["M001","MeasureTheory.tendsto_integral_of_dominated_convergence","Let A be any measurable space with measure μ and G any normed additive commutative group with a real normed vector-space structure. For F:ℕ→A→G, f:A→G and bound:A→ℝ, if each F(k) is μ-almost everywhere strongly measurable, bound is μ-integrable, ||F(k)(z)||≤bound(z) for μ-almost every z for every k, and F(k)(z)→f(z) as k→∞ for μ-almost every z, then ∫ F(k) dμ→∫ f dμ.",[b("A","measurable space"),b("μ","measure on A"),b("G","normed additive commutative group and real normed space"),b("F","sequence of functions A→G"),b("f","function A→G"),b("bound","function A→ℝ"),b("k","natural sequence index"),b("z","point of A")],["A","μ","G","F","f","bound","k","z"],["A is a measurable space, μ a measure, and G is a normed additive commutative group and real normed space.","Every F(k) is μ-almost everywhere strongly measurable.","bound is μ-integrable.","For each k, ||F(k)(z)||≤bound(z) for μ-almost every z.","For μ-almost every z, F(k)(z) tends to f(z)."]],
